  "question": {
    "text": "When a block moves down a smooth inclined plane of inclination <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>θ</mi></math>,&nbsp;its velocity on reaching the bottom is <math><mi>v</mi></math>. When&nbsp;it slides down a rough inclined plane of same inclination, its velocity on reaching the bottom is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></math>, where <math><mi>n</mi></math> is a number greater than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>. The coefficient of friction between the&nbsp;block and the rough surface is",
    "image": null
  },
